WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.010
My name is Seti, and I am a scribe living in Egypt in the year 1353 BC.

2
00:00:06.011 --> 00:00:14.397
A scribe is someone who reads and writes for people who cannot, and because not many people are literate, scribes are very valuable.

3
00:00:14.398 --> 00:00:19.690
We help government officials run the country and businessmen keep track of their goods.

4
00:00:19.691 --> 00:00:27.369
Scribes write down histories of great battles, the number of cattle in a herd, and anything else that needs to be remembered.

5
00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:32.354
To become a scribe, young boys usually have to be born into the profession.

6
00:00:32.355 --> 00:00:39.595
My father was a scribe, so I became one too, and at seven years old, I went to a palace school.

7
00:00:39.596 --> 00:00:44.555
Students sat around the teacher and sang songs to memorize different words,

8
00:00:44.556 --> 00:00:50.112
and after we learned the words, we would practice writing on pieces of broken pottery.

9
00:00:50.113 --> 00:00:54.576
If a student made a mistake, the teacher would hit him on the back with a stick and say,

10
00:00:54.577 --> 00:00:59.147
"A boy's ears are in his back—he will listen only when he is beaten!"

11
00:00:59.148 --> 00:01:05.605
Student scribes always made sure they knew their lessons well, if only to avoid the teacher's anger.

12
00:01:05.606 --> 00:01:13.895
It took me four years to learn how to read and write, and I learned to write in two different ways: hieroglyphic and hieratic.

13
00:01:13.896 --> 00:01:22.107
A hieroglyph is a picture that tells a reader what a word means, and each picture is a word or sound in the Egyptian language.

14
00:01:22.108 --> 00:01:27.492
A scribe must memorize and be able to write over seven hundred different pictures.

15
00:01:27.493 --> 00:01:34.654
Hieroglyphs are sacred, which means they are special to the gods, so they are used for tombs and monuments.

16
00:01:34.655 --> 00:01:40.291
For everyday communication, such as business letters, receipts, and government documents,

17
00:01:40.292 --> 00:01:46.558
we use hieratic writing, an alphabet of simple letters that are based on the hieroglyphs.

18
00:01:46.559 --> 00:01:54.216
After four years of school, I became an apprentice on the estate of a wealthy man who employed several scribes to keep his accounts.

19
00:01:54.217 --> 00:02:00.268
They taught me how to write his official letters and keep records of his possessions and trading activities.

20
00:02:00.269 --> 00:02:05.400
For example, I learned to write down the day, month, and season of each trade,

21
00:02:05.401 --> 00:02:10.625
what items were traded and received, and the name of the merchant involved in the transaction.

22
00:02:10.626 --> 00:02:20.814
I also had to carefully note the measure of what was traded whether it was a basket of grain, a jar of oil, a tall slave, or a large cow's head.

23
00:02:20.815 --> 00:02:26.377
Even though I wasn't paid, I gained a lot of experience working on a large estate.

24
00:02:26.378 --> 00:02:34.078
After my five-year apprenticeship, I was hired by the great pharaoh Amenhotep III as a scribe for the royal family.

25
00:02:34.079 --> 00:02:40.127
Amenhotep III has ruled Egypt for 37 years and has made our country very wealthy.

26
00:02:40.128 --> 00:02:43.203
He has ordered many statues and temples to be built,

27
00:02:43.204 --> 00:02:49.667
so scribes are needed to organize all the work and record all the supplies needed and used for the construction.

28
00:02:49.668 --> 00:02:55.728
In my position I write all the pharaoh's official letters to foreign kings in distant lands,

29
00:02:55.729 --> 00:03:01.390
and letters for royal family members who wish to keep in touch with relatives throughout the country.

30
00:03:01.391 --> 00:03:09.912
Every year scribes also write down how much grain has been grown and then calculate how long the grain will last after it is stored in the grain house.

31
00:03:09.913 --> 00:03:14.910
Storing grain can be difficult as fire, rats, and insects can be a problem,

32
00:03:14.911 --> 00:03:19.888
so the scribes must keep a careful tally of the grain as it sits in the grain house.

33
00:03:19.889 --> 00:03:27.422
In addition to recording agricultural matters, scribes read, copy, and archive all government documents, tax records,

34
00:03:27.423 --> 00:03:32.632
and the religious laws of the country each year to make sure the libraries are up-to-date.

35
00:03:32.633 --> 00:03:38.078
More than anyone else, scribes are very well-informed about the business of Egypt.

36
00:03:38.079 --> 00:03:43.117
Scribes are also hired to write magic prayers and the names of the deceased on their coffins.

37
00:03:43.118 --> 00:03:48.945
Egyptians believe that when a person dies, he or she lives on in an afterlife,

38
00:03:48.946 --> 00:03:56.420
so scribes write magical words to protect the spirits of the dead and to help the person find a path to the afterlife.

39
00:03:56.421 --> 00:04:00.607
These magical prayers have always been written in the pyramids for the pharaohs,

40
00:04:00.608 --> 00:04:05.253
but long ago scribes started writing coffin prayers for common people too.

41
00:04:05.254 --> 00:04:12.747
When I write, I use paper called papyrus, which is made from the stem of a reed that grows along the Nile River.

42
00:04:12.748 --> 00:04:18.107
The stem strips are cut, moistened, and layered on top of each other at right angles.

43
00:04:18.108 --> 00:04:22.184
Then they are pounded together and dried to make a sheet of paper.

44
00:04:22.185 --> 00:04:29.758
If I must write a long report, I paste the pages together to form a scroll that's rolled on two wooden handles.

45
00:04:29.759 --> 00:04:37.021
Sometimes I write on pottery, stone tablets, or parchment, which is made of animal hides stretched thin and dried.

46
00:04:37.022 --> 00:04:45.824
I have a wooden tablet called a palette with two holders for red and black ink, which is made with papyrus juice and another material for color.

47
00:04:45.825 --> 00:04:50.917
Red ink is made from red clay, and black ink is made from soot.

48
00:04:50.918 --> 00:04:57.279
The palette also holds my writing brush, which is made from the hollow stem of a grasslike plant called a rush.

49
00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:02.916
Before I can write with my brush, I chew on the end to soften it, so it can absorb the ink.

50
00:05:02.917 --> 00:05:07.320
The hieroglyph that stands for "scribe" is a picture of the equipment I use.

51
00:05:07.321 --> 00:05:17.011
Because of our ability to read and write, most people think scribes have mysterious powers from the gods, so we are treated well and get very rich.

52
00:05:17.012 --> 00:05:24.142
Because I'm a royal scribe, no one gives me orders except the pharaoh; therefore I don't have to do any hard work.

53
00:05:24.143 --> 00:05:30.548
The ability to read and write has given me a good life, but I feel sorry for the ordinary workers in the kingdom.

54
00:05:30.549 --> 00:05:37.517
Tired bodies and low pay are their only reward.

